 The desktop project references the original `SnowPakTool` project and calls its `CacheBlockReader`, `CacheBlockWriter`, and `ZipPakHelper` classes. It targets .NET 10 Windows Forms.
 
-The **Trucks-Cargo** tab lists cargo types and carrier variants from the active workspace, including DLC and sparse workspace updates. Search by cargo name, type, variant, or content pack; click column headers to sort. The table shows the defined cargo length, sum of addon physics body masses, and cargo value. Log cargo length represents carrier slots; body mass can include carrier parts. Blank numeric values mean the value is not explicitly defined. Select a row for its localized description and all attributes from the cargo type and addon source files. **Reload cargo** refreshes the workspace data after external edits. This catalog is read-only.
+The **Game data → Trucks-Cargo** sub-tab lists cargo types and carrier variants from the active workspace, including DLC and sparse workspace updates. Search by cargo name, type, variant, or content pack; click column headers to sort. The table shows the defined cargo length, sum of addon physics body masses, and cargo value. Log cargo length represents carrier slots; body mass can include carrier parts. Blank numeric values mean the value is not explicitly defined. Select a row for its localized description and all attributes from the cargo type and addon source files. **Reload cargo** refreshes the workspace data after external edits. This catalog is read-only.
 
 Packing keeps `[strings]` as top-level PAK content; only `[ps]` and `[ps_common]` are written into `initial.cache_block`. Regular assets use ZIP deflate compression (while `pak.load_list` and `.pct_header` files are stored) to avoid producing archives several times larger than the original.
